"P4024324979" "Joining the Pack"
// // requiresfailedtext :
"P0" ""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - TannerClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2985317576" "They went to the roof!"
// DetailString :
"P2519775027" "One of the hostages told you the following.<br><br><color gold>'You have to help Dr. Tanner, that Resistance madman, Ford, took him up onto the roof. He said they was going to make an example of him first!'</color><br><br>You'd better find a door to give you access to the roof quickly, there's no telling what this madman has in mind for Dr. Tanner."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ResistanceSuicideClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P579369823" "Suicide Mission"
// DetailString :
"P2269575703" "After taking Ford down you found a small audio device in one of his pockets. You flip it on and hear his voice say the following:<br><br><color paragon>To whatever chomper this is, you're probably tossin' a shadow over my corpse right now. If not, then you missed the party.<br><br>My name is... well... it was Ford, but nobody gives a puff what my real name was, so it doesn't float to ponder on it.<br><br>We red riding hooded into the Ministry of Technology knowin' we'd all get corpsed. So you must be grindin' gears as to why'd we do it.<br><br>We did it to send a big old message out to the sheeple here in Praetoria City. No matter how fluffy the names are, these government agencies doesn't work for you, they work to enslave you. Open your peepers and rub the sleep from 'em.<br><br>Can you even cogitate what went through our heads to do this? The hours and days we took reflecting on ourselves to come to the decision to deliver a message that only our corpses alone could deliver?<br><br>Or do you even know what happened to us? We brave few who took a jab against the emperor's stack of cards... did TPN even pipe this story into your brains?<br><br>Wake up! The gold and whitewash isn't that thick. Dig a little, and you'll find the dirt underneath, and the bodies this city is really built upon.<br><br>The wars are over, Cole. Give the people back the freedom they entrusted to you... or do you not trust us in return?<br><br></color><br><br>The message ends there."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - TeppClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P399146671" "Officer Tepp's Story"
// DetailString :
"P980309268" "Officer Tepp told you the following:<br><br><color gold>Sergeant Hastings lead the twelve of us down here looking for the Resistance. Well, we sure found 'em. We'd discovered one of their make shift bases and raided it. Sarge said he found some interesting intel on one of their computers, but on the way back up topside we got ambushed. Before I even knew what was going on, Sarge ordered me to head to the surface to call for help. Then Rounds, Hesh, and the Sarge all covered my escape. It wasn't until I got all the way up here that my comms started working again, so I called in for help. The Resistance found me not too long after, but then you showed up. Oh man, we've got to help the others!</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - GardenClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3296570303" "The Magisterium Gardens"
// DetailString :
"P3644004415" "The Magisterium Gardens are a work of art. Growing all manner of colorful flowers, amongst them, some yellow roses. People might not appreciate you taking some, but hey, you've got orders from the Praetor."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - RosesClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P13524022" "Synth Roses"
// DetailString :
"P3194942589" "These roses are beautiful, and thorn free to boot!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ChocolatesClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2340335224" "A Box of Chocolates"
// DetailString :
"P256080795" "It's only six pieces of chocolate, but this is the good stuff."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CleopatraMadClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P713431281" "Cleopatra"
// DetailString :
"P2190762233" "Hell hath no fury...<br><br>You don't know what Praetor White did to get on Cleopatra's bad side, but you're glad she didn't kill the messenger. Actually, as long as you're not the Praetor, she seems like a pretty fun lady."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CleopatraFlirtyClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1325027586" "You can see why Praetor White like Cleopatra. She's smart, sassy, and fun. Of course, something tells you that she's got a really rough streak in her if she can keep the man once known as Marauder on a leash tight enough to make him give her gifts."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DuvalClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3743959590" "Captain Duval said chomp?"
// DetailString :
"P1951954514" "You weren't too surprised that the PPD jumped you when push came to shove, but you get a sneaking suspicion that Duval would never say "chomp". It appears that the PPD officers inspecting Gravatech Labs aren't police officers at all, they're Resistance imposters!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ResistancePlotClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2985194397" "Resistance Plot"
// DetailString :
"P703879134" "From the looks of it the resistance were planning on creating a distraction so that their PPD imposters could effortlessly walk into a number of important government offices and raid them for sensitive material as well. It's a good thing you stopped them because the average citizen knows better than to question the actions of the PPD."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - StolenDataClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P215265156" "Stolen Gravatech Data"
// DetailString :
"P605408193" "You found this stolen Gravatech Labs data on the imposter posing as Justicar Easton. It would seem that the theft of the Gravatech Labs data was basically a field test to see if their disguises would work. If you hadn't shown up, they very well might have."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - JoiningThePackClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P954711551" "Joining the Pack"
// tDetailString :
"P2065793041" "You remember all too well the slap on the shoulder that Praetor White gave you after you proved yourself to him through a process he called...<br><br><color Gold>Joining The Pack</color><br><br>In the aftermath of the Resistance attack on PPD Precinct 5 you reported to Praetor White as instructed. The big man was annoyed by the phyrric victory the PPD had managed to pull off against the Resistance attack. But he was even more disturbed that the entire affair turned out to be a diversion to allow a Resistance strike team to infiltrate the Ministry of Technology and take some of the leading scientists hostage. He sent you in to disarm the situation without leveling the entire building, but when you took down the Resistance fighters you discovered that they had no intention of leaving the building alive.<br><br>With the PPD patrols in the tunnels tripled it didn't take long for them to stumble into more than they could handle. You were ordered to come to the rescue of a PPD search team lead by Sergeant Hastings. When you found Hastings he informed you that he had critical information regarding Resistance plans to attack the Ministry of Information.<br><br>With the Resistance plans foiled for the time being, Praetor White gave you a task of a more personal nature: getting some flowers for his lady, Cleopatra. At first you thought it might be a joke, but after hunting the flowers down and then delivering them to Cleopatra you understand why keeping her happy is in his best interest.<br><br>With the Praetor warming up to you and your no-nonsense style, he gave you the responsibility of inspecting Gravatech Labs. The only caveat was that the PPD were there overstepping the Praetor's jurisdiction with a surprise inspection of their own. You went into the laboratory to remind Captain Duval of where his jurisdiction ended and the Praetor's began, but it turns out that Duval and his entire entourage of PPD officers were actually Resistance fighters in disguise. After foiling their plot to steal sensitive information from the lab's databases you returned to Praetor White and were recognized as a member of his pack."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P662221039" "This day just gets better and better!<br><br>We lost a lot of officers during the Resistance attack on Precinct 5 earlier. Then, to make matters worse, the dumb-as-dirt TPN media circus decides it would be a good idea to report on it and spin the pyrrhic victory into a 'crushing victory over the terrorists' center piece in today's news, so now a riot's broken out here in the Magisterium!<br><br>But to top it all off the Resistance used the battle as a distraction to get at their true objective, <color orange>they've taken hostages in the Ministry of Technology.</color><br><br>I need you to get in there and rescue those hostages before someone important gets killed."
// AcceptString :
"P3829363570" "Rescue the Hostages"
// SendOffString :
"P2385514374" "I just can't believe how lax the PPD have gotten without us around. Well, maybe you can show them how it's done.<br><br>You know, I'd go in there and take care of it myself, I even have half a mind to do so anyway, but Cleo is right; I'd end up killing every coward in there and level the building, and that wouldn't do us any favors right now winning back the trust of the people."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3856792041" "Rescue Hostages in the Ministry of Technology"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3903710169" "I'm pretty sure those terrorists aren't going to stick around all day. If I were you I'd be in there busting heads right now. So get to it!"
// TaskTitle :
"P742779165" "<color deepskyblue>Joining The Pack</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P3595810709" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: Acts of Desperation</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2794050679" "The Ministry of Technology is quieter than normal, though you can hear muffled voices shouting somewhere up ahead."

